INT. CORPORATE MASCOT COSTUME ROOM - DAY

A windowless closet crowded with oversized plush heads on shelves. A giant foam taco, a giant foam toaster, a lion with one eye missing. A speaker on the wall crackles.

DUNCAN ALBRIGHT, 50s, regional marketing manager, tapped-out and pacing, shoves a mannequin aside. In the doorway stands an INTERN, 20s, in an oversized lanyard, holding a clipboard and a lukewarm coffee.

DUNCAN
Who are you?

INTERN
I'm the, um, intern.

DUNCAN
I've never seen you before.

INTERN
I started Monday.

DUNCAN
It's Thursday.

INTERN
I know.

DUNCAN
Come in, come in. Close the door.

The Intern closes it. The room shrinks. Duncan rummages through the costumes, pulls out a hulking toaster head, and tosses it to the Intern.

DUNCAN (CONT'D)
Put that on.

INTERN
Why?

DUNCAN
Because Brian called in sick, and the parade starts at noon.

INTERN
I'm not trained for this.

DUNCAN
It's a toaster. It pops up.

The wall speaker crackles to life. A brisk female voice fills the closet.

MS. VANDERHOOF (V.O.)
Duncan. I'm told the toaster is missing.

DUNCAN
(to the speaker)
It's being handled, Ms. Vanderhoof.

MS. VANDERHOOF (V.O.)
By whom?

DUNCAN
(glancing at the Intern)
By... Kiran.

INTERN
Kiran?

DUNCAN
(sotto)
It's what's on your lanyard.

The Intern checks the tag. It does say KIRAN SETHI in tiny type. Kiran puts the toaster head on. A muffled voice emerges.

KIRAN
(muffled)
This smells like feet.

MS. VANDERHOOF (V.O.)
Is Kiran ready?

KIRAN
(muffled)
Kiran is as ready as Kiran will ever be.

DUNCAN
Excellent. Go pop.

Kiran waddles out the door and collides with the frame. The toaster head falls off and rolls across the floor. Duncan buries his face in his hands.

MS. VANDERHOOF (V.O.)
I heard that.
